id: decisions/051-closed-with-named-openings
title: "Closed schemas, openings named and typed"
kind: decision-frame
record_shape: header
status: draft
authored_by: agent-on-behalf
authored_via: "Claude Code session on Dave's behalf, 2026-09-12; drafted from the JUDGMENTS.md reversal axis 'schema-strictness'; recommendation is an attributed inference and ratifies nothing"
version: "1.0.0"
updated: 2026-09-12
template_ref: templates/decision.yawn
principal_ref: principal:dave

axis: schema-strictness
axis_gloss: "whether a schema rejects everything it does not name, or tolerates unknown keys for forward compatibility"
poles:
  a: closed-world-schema
  b: open-extensible-schema
split: lone-exception
draft_status: full
leverage: 1.6
leverage_formula: "judgments_resolved(4) x split_weight(0.4) x authored_conflict_bonus(1)"

question: >
  Should every schema reject keys it does not name, including inside event
  payloads and proof pre/postconditions, or are there named places where a
  record may carry open content?

why_it_matters: >
  All 29 schemas close every object they name, yet payload, preconditions and
  postconditions are bare untyped objects and two nested sites are open, so the
  strictness has holes nobody has listed. Once answered, a bot that emits an
  event knows whether its payload must declare what it is, and a child Yawn
  inherits schemas whose extension points are known rather than discovered.

state_snapshot:
  description: >
    3 judgments sit at closed-world-schema (0 authored) and 1 at
    open-extensible-schema (0 authored). The repository asserts both directions on
    this axis.
  attributed_to: JUDGMENTS.md
  epistemic_status: observed
  source_refs:
    - JUDGMENTS.md
    - TAXONOMY.md

lacuna:
  kind: unselected_choice
  description: >
    Whether schemas/statuses.v1.schema.json, closed and satisfied by no record, is
    to be adopted or retired; that bears on how much closure the repo can actually
    afford.

options:
  - name: A
    description: >
      rule: Every schema is closed everywhere. payload, preconditions and
      postconditions receive typed shapes; the two additionalProperties: true sites
      in agency-holarchy.v0.2 and objective-holon.v0.1 are closed.
    cost: "Type every event payload by eventType; extend tests/observation-state-v1.test.mjs and tests/state-substrate-v1.test.mjs; risk breaking the two open sites' 24 passing assertions."
    risk: "A closed payload schema must be revised for every new event type, and unknown fields are lost on round-trip; schemas/statuses.v1 shows a closed schema nobody adopts is dead weight (GROUND_TRUTH FACT 2)."
    reversibility: false
    proof_needed: "A test in tests/ that no schema in schemas/ contains additionalProperties: true or an object with no properties."
    evidence_for:
      - "J1061"
      - "J1138"
      - "J1208"
  - name: B
    description: >
      rule: Schemas are open by default so unanticipated fields survive round-trips;
      additionalProperties is true or omitted unless a field must be rejected.
    cost: "Rewrite 29 schemas and the 128 assertions that rely on fail-closed behaviour."
    risk: "Typo'd keys pass silently; the hand-written fail-closed date-time format (J1208) becomes the odd one out."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "None; the test suite's fail-closed assertions would be removed."
    evidence_for:
      - "J1112"
  - name: C
    description: >
      rule: Schemas are closed by default. Open content is allowed only at named
      extension points, listed in schemas/node.yawn: event payload, record-event
      payload, proof-receipt preconditions and postconditions, and the two existing
      additionalProperties: true sites. Each open site carries a required
      discriminator (payloadType or schemaRef) so the open object still says what it
      is. A new open site outside the list is a defect.
    cost: "Add the list to schemas/node.yawn; add a required discriminator to event.v1, record-event.v1 and record-proof-receipt; one test."
    risk: "The list grows by exception until closed-by-default is nominal."
    reversibility: true
    proof_needed: "A test in tests/ that greps schemas/*.json for additionalProperties: true and for objects with no properties, and fails unless each site is on the allowlist in schemas/node.yawn and carries the discriminator."
    evidence_for:
      - "J1061"
      - "J1138"
      - "J1208"

recommendation:
  option_ref: C
  confidence: 0.7
  epistemic_status: inferred
  authority: none
  reasoning: >
    All four judgments are revealed, but the closed side is behaviour-proven
    across 29 schemas and the whole 128-assertion suite, including a deliberately
    hand-written fail-closed date-time format. The one open judgment is not a
    preference but a hole: payload objects with no shape in schemas that close
    everything else. A payload whose shape varies by event type is a legitimate
    extension point, so removing it (A) is the wrong fix; leaving it untyped is
    not the same as making it open on purpose. C keeps closed-by-default and makes
    the openings explicit and self-describing. The unused statuses.v1 schema (FACT
    2) is the cautionary case for A.

target_condition:
  mode: decide
  proposed_by: agent-on-behalf
  affected_principals:
    - principal:dave
  ratification_status: proposed
  sufficient_when:
    - "schemas/node.yawn lists the open extension points by schema and property."
    - "A test in tests/ fails when a new open object appears outside that list, and passes."
    - "event.v1 and record-event.v1 payloads require a discriminator keyed to eventType."

choice:
  selected_by: ""
  option_ref: ""
  authority_ref: ""

proof:
  covers:
    - target_condition
    - options
  falsifier: >
    A third additionalProperties: true appears in schemas/ and no test notices.
  status: proposed

resolves:
  - "J1061"
  - "J1138"
  - "J1208"
  - "J1112"

boundary:
  - "confidence cannot ratify an objective; this record proposes and Dave decides"
  - "the REVEALED judgments cited here describe what artifacts do, not what Dave chose"

source:
  template: templates/decision.yawn
  axis: TAXONOMY.md
  inventory: JUDGMENTS.md
